From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 16:52:46 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] SWGL on Windows 10 Mobile: pixel shaders made at idle, what
 the device refused, partial redraw with a video

The 9_3 pixel shaders were created on each program's first draw, inside that
frame, and one the driver refused was only counted. Some seconds after the
first GPU-shaded frame, at idle, the shaders no draw has needed yet are now
created a few milliseconds at a time between frames (largest first, a crash
guard file skipping one that brought the process down), and the log says how
many the device accepted and which it refused, with the reason. The device
line gains format support and driver features. The compositor's composite
after a video frame now covers WebRender's dirty area and the video's rect
instead of the whole window (gfx.webrender.gecko-w10m.video-whole-window
brings the old way back), and upload-mode is ignored while GPU shading is
on, where it would have made tiles with no texture.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
